      "type": "ai_explain",
      "question_type": "explain",
      "task_kind": "explain",
      "character": {
        "emotion": "curious",
        "say": {
          "en": "When n = 4, why is 3n equal to 12 and not 34? Can you teach me?",
          "ur": "جب n = 4 ہو تو 3n کا جواب 12 کیوں ہے، 34 کیوں نہیں؟ کیا آپ مجھے سکھا سکتے ہیں؟"
        }
      },
      "task": {
        "en": "In your own words: when n = 4, why is 3n equal to 12 and not 34?",
        "ur": "اپنے الفاظ میں بتائیں: جب n = 4 ہو تو 3n کا جواب 12 کیوں ہے، 34 کیوں نہیں؟"
      },
      "key_idea": "In algebra, a number written next to a letter means multiply: 3n means 3 × n. So with n = 4 it is 3 × 4 = 12. 34 would be thirty-four, which is not what 3n means.",
      "levels": {
        "got_it": "Explains that 3n means 3 × n, so it is 3 × 4 = 12, and that writing the digits side by side gives a different number.",
